          ":question/problem": "Which of the following are row vectors?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -4 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -1 & 3 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is *not* a row vector, since it has more than $1$ row (it has $3$ rows).\n\n- $B$ is a row vector since it has only one row.\n\n- $C$ is *not* a row vector. It has only one column (and $4$ rows), so it's a column vector.\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is a row vector.",
